m runbook, I rolled checkout-api back to the most recent healthy release, v2.3.0, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Release history: v2.2.9 healthy, v2.3.0 healthy, v2.3.1-rc unhealthy, v2.3.1 unhealthy. Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. Next steps: confirm sustained recovery on v2.3.0 and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with the error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks, so I chose v2.3.0 as the most recent healthy release. It had a healthy production history, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the SEV2 incident timed out. I checked the incident list, found nothing had been created, and retried once. That created **INC-0002**, which is open and has paged on-call. The summary covers the rollback and the next steps: confirm recovery holds on v2.3.0 and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "type": "text"}]}]}